title: >-
  From the Political Behavior Archive to the Data Science Center:
  An institutional history of UCLA's social science data archive, 1961-2026
message: "If you cite this work, please use the metadata in this file."
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Dennis
    given-names: Tim
    affiliation: "UCLA Library, Data Science Center"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6632-3812"
  - family-names: Jamison
    given-names: Jina "Jamie"
    affiliation: "UCLA Library, Data Science Center"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5116-5724"
abstract: >-
  An institutional history of one continuous function at UCLA - the stewardship
  of research data - traced across six decades and five institutional homes:
  from the Political Behavior Archive (founded 1961 by Dwaine Marvick), through
  the Survey Research Center and the Institute for Social Science Research, the
  1977 naming of the Social Science Data Archive, the 2014 transfer to the UCLA
  Library, and the 2018 formation of the Data Science Center. Written by the
  unit's director as a legacy record, emphasizing the continuity of the function
  across changes of name, home, and scope.
keywords:
